        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source>
                "HSE Incident Management Framework - Guidance 2020" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition>
                "The National Incident Report Form (NIRF) was developed by the State Claims Agency in conjunction with all stakeholders including the HSE and voluntary hospitals. Use of a NIRF assures the accuracy of data and clarity of information being reported. There are four forms in total; Person, Property, Crash/Collision and Dangerous Occurrences/Reportable Circumstance i.e. Dangerous Occurrences/Reportable Circumstances." ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme>
                <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#> ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note>
                "HSE Incident Management Framework - Guidance 2020" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel>
                "National Incident Reporting Form" .

<https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Effective>
        a       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created>
                "18/12/2020" ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator>
                "Lucy" ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source>
                "HSE Incident Management Framework - Guidance 2020 / HIQA National Standards for the Prevention and Control of Healthcare-Associated Infections 2017" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition>
                "A measure of the extent to which a specific intervention, procedure, treatment or service, when delivered, does what is intended for a specific population." ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme>
                <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#> ;
