                "A product, except medicines, used in healthcare to diagnose, prevent, monitor or treat illness or disability" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme>
                <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#> ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower>
                <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#MedicalDeviceEquipmentDecontaminationCommittee> , <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#InvasiveMedicalDevice> , <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#SingleUseItem> , <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#ReusableInvasiveMedicalDevice> ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note>
                "HIQA National Standards for the Prevention and Control of Healthcare-Associated Infections 2017" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel>
                "Medical Device" .

<https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#HealthServiceExecutive>
        a       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created>
                "19/05/21" ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator>
                "Lucy" ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source>
                "HIQA National Standards for the Prevention and Control of Healthcare-Associated Infections 2017" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition>
                "Provider and or funder of all of Ireland’s public acute healthcare services or any subsequent agency that takes on the HSE’s statutory functions" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme>
                <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#> ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower>
                <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#HSEIntegratedRiskManagementPolicyAndGuidanceDocuments> , <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#HSEIncidentManagementFramework> ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note>
                "HIQA National Standards for the Prevention and Control of Healthcare-Associated Infections 2017" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel>
                "Health Service Executive (HSE)" .

<https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#StrategicRisk>
        a       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created>
                "7/9/20" ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator>
                "Rob" ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source>
                "HSE Integrated Risk Management Policy - Part 1/ISO 31000:2009" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition>
                "A strategic risk has the ability to impact on the achievement/delivery of the HSE’s strategic objectives/directions. Strategic risks relate to the highest level of objective for the HSE, which typically have a long-term focus and are linked to the HSE’s Strategic Plan." ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme>
                <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#> ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note>
                "HSE Integrated Risk Management Policy - Part 1/ISO 31000:2009" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel>
                "Strategic Risk" .

<https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#CorporateGovernance>
        a       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created>
                "19/05/21" ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator>
                "Lucy" ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source>
                "HIQA National Standards for the Prevention and Control of Healthcare-Associated Infections 2017" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition>
                "The system by which services direct and control their functions in order to achieve organisational objectives, manage their business processes, meet required standards of accountability, integrity and propriety and relate to external stakeholders" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme>
                <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#> ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note>
                "HIQA National Standards for the Prevention and Control of Healthcare-Associated Infections 2017" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel>
                "Corporate Governance" .

<https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Staff>
        a       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created>
                "18/12/2020" ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator>
                "Lucy" ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source>
                "HSE Incident Management Framework 2020 / HSE Incident Management Framework - Guidance 2020" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition>
                "(a) a person who(i) has entered into, or works under (or where the employment has ceased, had entered into or worked under), a contract of employment, with the health services provider, or(ii) is (or was) placed for the purpose of vocational training with the health services provider, and(b) a fixed-term employee of the health services provider, and a reference to an employee, in relation to a health services provider, shall be construed as a reference to an employee employed by that health services provider.In line with the definition of Employee as defined in the (Civil Liability Amendment Act, 2017)" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme>
                <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#> ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower>
                <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#StaffLiaisonPerson> , <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#StaffConsultation> ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note>
                "HSE Incident Management Framework 2020 / HSE Incident Management Framework - Guidance 2020" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel>
                "Staff" .

<https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Infection>
        a       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created>
                "19/05/21" ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator>
                "Lucy" ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source>
                "HIQA National Standards for the Prevention and Control of Healthcare-Associated Infections 2017" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition>
                "The invasion and reproduction of pathogenic or disease-causing micro-organisms inside the body that may cause tissue injury and disease" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme>
                <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#> ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower>
                <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#IncidenceOfInfection> , <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#InfectionPreventionAndControl> , <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#HealthcareAssociatedInfection> , <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Sepsis> , <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PostExposureProphylaxis> ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note>
                "HIQA National Standards for the Prevention and Control of Healthcare-Associated Infections 2017" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel>
                "Infection" .

<https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#ConcernsAndEnquiries>
        a       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created>
                "18/12/2020" ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator>
                "Lucy" ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source>
                "HSE Incident Management Framework - Guidance 2020" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition>
                "A concern or enquiry is a problem raised that can be resolved/responded to straight away, (by the end of the next working day). These are not reported as complaints and fall outside the complaints management arrangements" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme>
                <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#> ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note>
                "HSE Incident Management Framework - Guidance 2020" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel>
                "Concerns and Enquiries" .
